		<div class="texto-blog">					
		<p>In this article we will see <strong>how to block adblock in symfony 5 framework</strong> on our website, we will use the library <strong>SweetAlert2</strong> to create elegant alerts, we will first start from a script that this friend shares with us in his <a class="" href="https://jonathanmelgoza.com/blog/como-detectar-adblock-con-javascript/" target="_blank">publication</a>, which I found interesting, always remember to give credit to other people's work.</p>

		<h2>How to avoid Adblock on my website?</h2>

		{{ include('inc/ad_defect.html.twig') }} 	
		
		<p>Many people make a living from their web projects, be it a blog, referral links etc, the use of <strong>Adblock</strong> limits the presence of advertisements on our website, with the use of <strong>Google AdSense</strong>.</p>

		<p>first we start from <strong>script</strong> base of the friend, which generates a generic alert when detecting the blocker, what we will do is create an alert with which the user will not be able to remove the alert when clicking, until <strong>disable blocker</strong>.</p>

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
        $(document).ready(function(){
 
          detectarBloqueador();
 
        });

        async function detectarBloqueador(){
          const bloqueadorActivo = await checkAdBlocker();
          if( bloqueadorActivo ){
          	  
              // we will create a new function, upon detecting the blocker 
              modalBlock();
          }
      }

      async function checkAdBlocker() {
 
          let bloqueador;
       
          async function tryRequest() {
              try {
                 return fetch(
                     new Request("https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js", {
                        method: 'HEAD',
                        mode: 'no-cors'
                      }))
                      .then(function(response) {
                        bloqueador = false;
                        return bloqueador;
                      }).catch(function(e) {
                        bloqueador = true;
                        return bloqueador;
                  });
              } catch (error) {
                    console.log(error);
                    bloqueador = true;
                    return bloqueador;
              }
          }
       
          return bloqueador !== undefined ? bloqueador : await tryRequest();
      }           
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>So far what we have done is add a new function called <code>modalBlock()</code>, now we proceed with the loading of the jquery and sweetalert libraries with the use of their cdn.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/alert1.png" alt="alert1">

		</div>

		<h2>How to use sweetalert 2?</h2>

		<p>We will then call the function <code>modalBlock()</code>, remember to open and close script tag, we will use the function <code>swal()</code> which inside has properties such as icon, title, etc., we will use the property <strong>button</strong> as false so that a button does not appear and here the important thing is the property <strong>closeOnClickOutside</strong>, so that when clicking outside the modal it does not close.</p>

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
		async function modalBlock()
		{

		    swal({
		      icon: "warning",
		      title: 'Este sitio muestra anuncios',
		      text: 'DeshabilitarAdBlock',
		      type: 'warning',
		      showCancelButton: false,
		      showConfirmButton: false,
		      button: false,
		      closeOnClickOutside: false
		    }).then(function() {      

		    	console.log("Algun mensaje de success,opcional");

		      }, function(err) {   

		      	console.log("Algun mensaje de error" + err);
		      });

		  }          
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>Result when we have adblock activated.</p>

